            <ArticleTitle>Left main coronary artery aneurysm: an uncommon aetiology for myocardial infarction in the young.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>584-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S1047951110000910</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Left main coronary artery aneurysms are very infrequent (0.1%) and the majority is related to atherosclerotic obstructive lesions. We describe a young male having no conventional coronary risk factors presenting with acute inferior wall myocardial infarction. Coronary angiography revealed a prominent aneurysm of the left main coronary artery with selective extension towards the proximal left circumflex artery without associated coronary lesions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
